        <p class="lede">
          The Orgain protein powder Costco sells is the 2.74 lb tub of Organic Protein Plant-Based Powder, about 27 two-scoop servings of 21 g of protein. Multiply the price on your warehouse tag by 0.044 to get its cost per 25 g of protein. What changes the verdict is the dose, the flavor you pick and the July 2026 class action over lead, which this page lays out allegation by allegation.
        </p>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Costco Orgain Protein Powder: The Short Answer
          </h2>

          <p>
            Costco's Orgain is a good-value organic plant protein but a mid-priced protein once you adjust for its small 21 g dose. The 2.74 lb tub holds roughly 1,243 g of powder, which at 46 g a serving is about 27 servings and about 567 g of protein in total, per the label at the time of writing. That is why the tag price alone misleads: a $25 tub of Orgain and a $50 bag of Kirkland whey are not close to the same deal.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-4">The 2.74 lb Tub by the Numbers</p>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 text-center">
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-white">~27</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Two-scoop servings</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-[#38BDF8]">21 g</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Protein per serving</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-white">x 0.044</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Tag price to cost per 25 g</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-[#38BDF8]">143%</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Consumer Reports lead level of concern (Vanilla Bean, 2025)</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p>
            The lawsuit is real but unresolved. Seven consumers sued Costco, not Orgain, in federal court in Seattle in July 2026, claiming Costco should have disclosed lead, cadmium and arsenic in two Orgain flavors. Costco has asked the judge to dismiss the case. No court has found the powder unsafe, and there has been no recall that we could find.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="which-orgain" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. Which Orgain Protein Powders Does Costco Sell?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Costco's core Orgain item is the USDA Organic Plant-Based Protein Powder in a 2.74 lb tub, usually in Vanilla Bean and Creamy Chocolate Fudge. That is the same pea, brown rice and chia blend sold in supermarkets, just in a bigger container: the standard retail tub is 2.03 lb, so the Costco size holds about a third more powder. Costco.com listings also show seasonal flavors in the same 2.74 lb size, such as Peppermint Hot Cocoa, and deal posts from past years show Pumpkin Spice, so the flavor on the shelf in your warehouse may not match what your friend saw last month.
          </p>

          <p>
            Costco has also listed Orgain Organic Protein and Superfoods, a version that adds a powdered blend of fruits, vegetables and grains, in tubs of about 2.6 to 2.7 lb. Costco Business Delivery lists it at 21 g of protein per serving, the same dose as the regular tub. The superfoods are present in small amounts, so treat them as a flavor and marketing difference rather than a reason to pay more, and compare the two on cost per gram of protein before choosing.
          </p>

          <p>
            What Costco generally does not stock is the rest of the Orgain range. The 30 g Organic Vegan Protein (sold as Orgain Sport in some stores), the Grass-Fed Whey and the Simple line with coconut sugar are easier to find on Amazon, at Target or on Orgain's own site. If you want one of those, our <a href="/orgain-protein-powder-review/">Orgain protein powder review</a> compares all four tubs on dose, sweetener and price.
          </p>

          <p>
            Orgain ready-to-drink shakes are a separate product. Costco has run its Orgain coupons across both powders and shakes, per a December 2023 deal report, so check which item a discount covers before you assume it applies to the tub. The lawsuit described below names the powders, specifically the Vanilla Bean and Creamy Chocolate Fudge flavors, and not the shakes.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
